      "widgets_values": [
        "DEMO: Read the result contract, without AI. The Decision Scores Validator checks supplied example numbers and the selected label. The Text / JSON Viewer displays the validated answer. We supplied these scores; they were not inferred. Blue and orange are allowed labels. Editing the fixture tests consistency, not training. Read Tutorial 0 first.\n\n1. Press top Run. The validator checks the supplied fixture.\n2. Open scores in the viewer Tree mode. Blue has the larger score and is selected.\n3. Optional experiment: change blue to 0.1, keep orange at 0.2, AND change \"choice\":\"blue\" to \"choice\":\"orange\" in the same JSON. Run again: orange wins. Editing scores alone does not update choice.\n4. The scores need not sum to 1. The viewer normalizes 0.1/0.2 to about 0.333/0.667. This checks a supplied answer; it does not train a model. In model demos, edit the situation instead.\n\nNodes in this demo:\nꘅ Decision Scores Validator · supplied decision fixture (no AI)\nꘅ Text / JSON Viewer · 2 · normalized scores\nꘅ Text / JSON Viewer · 3 · selected choice"
      ]
    },
